# Notebooks

This folder contains Jupyter notebooks used in the AI-guided Hantaan virus
(HTNV) L-protein/RdRp inhibitor-discovery project.

## Project Focus

The project focuses on computational inhibitor discovery for the Hantaan virus
(HTNV) L-protein/RNA-dependent RNA polymerase (RdRp), using the experimental
structure PDB 8C4T.

## Workflow

1. FDA-approved compound library preparation.
2. Virtual screening and docking-based prioritization.
3. ADMET profiling and drug-likeness analysis.
4. Lead identification, with baloxavir used as the lead scaffold.
5. Bemis–Murcko scaffold analysis.
6. Reaction-based analogue generation using SMIRKS and SELFIES.
7. Generative analogue design using REINVENT.
8. Scaffold hopping across 10 scaffold classes.
9. Molecular similarity analysis.
10. Docking-score analysis for HTNV 8C4T and exploratory tubulin–colchicine-site target PDB 1SA0.
11. Residue-level interaction analysis.
12. Explainable AI analysis using SHAP and GNNExplainer.
13. Pharmacophore modeling and visualization.

## Key Candidates

- **Gen2_Trifluoromethyl** — prioritized Gen-2 analogue, with a predicted docking score of −8.649 kcal/mol against HTNV 8C4T.
- **Analog_2A_Indole** and **Analog_3B_Quinoline** — HTNV-retained profile candidates.
- **Analog_7A_Coumarin**, **Analog_7B_Coumarin**, and **Analog_10B_Biphenyl** — exploratory dual-target profile candidates.

## Important Note

All outputs are computational predictions and are hypothesis-generating only.
No molecular-dynamics simulations or experimental validation were performed in
the present study.
